# PROJECT OVERVIEW
# Restaurant Customer Behavior — Statistical & Probabilistic Analysis Dashboard

---

## 1. PROJECT DESCRIPTION

This is a **fully client-side, interactive Mathematics & Statistics web application** built for
academic and analytical purposes. It performs a comprehensive **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)**
on the Seaborn *tips* dataset — 244 real restaurant transactions recorded at a US diner —
converted to **Indian Rupees (INR, ₹)** at a fixed exchange rate of **1 USD = ₹83.00**.

The project acts as both:
- A **learning tool** demonstrating core Probability & Statistics concepts (central tendency,
  dispersion, outlier detection, empirical probability, correlation)
- A **business intelligence dashboard** that translates raw data into actionable restaurant
  management recommendations via an embedded AI report generator

All statistical computations are implemented from scratch in pure JavaScript (no statistical
library used) and the dashboard updates reactively whenever filters are applied or new data
is uploaded.

---

## 2. PURPOSE OF THE PROJECT

- **Academic goal:** Satisfy a Mathematics/Statistics course project requirement covering:
  - Data types & scales of measurement
  - Measures of central tendency (Mean, Median, Mode)
  - Measures of dispersion (Range, IQR, Standard Deviation, CV)
  - Box plot & outlier analysis (Tukey's IQR Rule)
  - Data visualizations (7 required chart types, no KDE)
  - Empirical probability & conditional probability
  - Pearson correlation coefficient
- **Practical goal:** Create a reusable EDA dashboard that works with any CSV file matching
  the expected schema, giving restaurant owners or analysts a real-time data exploration tool.
- **Presentation goal:** Generate a formatted Word document (`Project_Demonstration.docx`) to
  hand in alongside the web app.

---

## 3. TECHNOLOGY STACK

### Frontend (Web Application)
| Layer       | Technology                        | Version / Source                          |
|-------------|-----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|
| Markup      | HTML5                             | Semantic, SEO-compliant                   |
| Styling     | Vanilla CSS3                      | Custom, no frameworks                     |
| Logic       | Vanilla JavaScript (ES2020+)      | No build step, runs directly in browser   |
| Charts      | **Chart.js**                      | v4.4.1 via jsDelivr CDN                   |
| CSV Parsing | **PapaParse**                     | v5.4.1 via cdnjs CDN                      |
| Icons       | **FontAwesome**                   | v6.4.0 via cdnjs CDN                      |
| Typography  | **Google Fonts**                  | Plus Jakarta Sans + JetBrains Mono        |

### Backend / Data Analysis (Python)
| Layer              | Technology        | Purpose                                           |
|--------------------|-------------------|---------------------------------------------------|
| Data manipulation  | **pandas**        | DataFrame operations, groupby, stats              |
| Numerical math     | **NumPy**         | polyfit (linear regression), array ops            |
| Dataset source     | **seaborn**       | `sns.load_dataset('tips')` — embedded dataset     |
| Plotting           | **matplotlib**    | Generates 7 static PNG charts + 1 composite       |
| DOCX generation    | **python-docx**   | Generates `Project_Demonstration.docx`            |

### AI / LLM Integration (Business Report Tab)
| Provider       | Model                          | Role               |
|----------------|--------------------------------|--------------------|
| Google Gemini  | `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`        | Primary AI engine  |
| OpenRouter     | `meta-llama/llama-3.1-8b-instruct:free` | Fallback #1 |
| Groq           | `llama3-8b-8192`               | Fallback #2        |

Calls are made via browser `fetch()` to public REST APIs. The fallback chain is tried
sequentially if any provider returns an error or is blocked by CORS.

---

## 4. DATASET DETAILS

- **Source:** Seaborn built-in `tips` dataset
- **Records:** n = 244 dining parties (observations)
- **Features:** 7 variables
- **Currency conversion:** total_bill and tip multiplied by ₹83.00
- **CSV schema (7 columns):**

```
total_bill, tip, sex, smoker, day, time, size
```

### Variable Classification Matrix

| Variable     | Broad Type    | Statistical Sub-type | Scale of Measurement | Description                          |
|--------------|---------------|----------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------|
| `total_bill` | Quantitative  | Continuous           | Ratio                | Cost of meal in ₹ INR                |
| `tip`        | Quantitative  | Continuous           | Ratio                | Tip/gratuity amount in ₹ INR         |
| `size`       | Quantitative  | Discrete             | Ratio                | Number of diners at the table (1–6)  |
| `sex`        | Qualitative   | Nominal              | Nominal              | Gender of the bill payer (Male/Female) |
| `smoker`     | Qualitative   | Nominal              | Nominal              | Smoking party in group? (Yes/No)     |
| `day`        | Qualitative   | Nominal              | Nominal              | Day of week (Thur/Fri/Sat/Sun)       |
| `time`       | Qualitative   | Nominal              | Nominal              | Meal service time (Lunch/Dinner)     |

