## 7. UI TABS — DETAILED WALKTHROUGH

### Tab 1 · Overview & Data Types
- **Variable Type Hierarchy table:** 7 variables × 4 columns (Type, Sub-type, Scale, Description)
- **Statistical Concept Reference accordion:** 3 expandable concept boxes (Qual vs Quant, Discrete vs Continuous, Scales of Measurement)
- **Interactive Customer Records Explorer:** Full paginated, sortable, searchable raw data table
  - Columns: #, Total Bill, Tip, Tip%, Sex, Smoker, Day, Time, Party Size
  - Sorting: click any column header to toggle ascending/descending
  - Search: live filter across bill values, day, sex, time
  - Pagination: 10 rows per page with Prev/Next buttons

### Tab 2 · Central Tendency & Dispersion
- **Formula banner:** Scrollable strip showing 5 formulas (Mean, Median, Range, IQR, CV)
- **Three metric blocks** (one per numeric variable): Total Bill, Tip, Party Size
  - Each block shows: Mean, Median, Mode | Range, Q1, Q3 | IQR, StdDev, CV
  - Skewness indicator badge at bottom
- **Day-Wise Variability table:** Thur/Fri/Sat/Sun × 10 metrics (Count, Mean, Median, StdDev, Q1, Q3, IQR, Range, CV, Variability Level badge)
- Variability insight alert box: identifies highest and lowest CV days

### Tab 3 · Box Plot & Outlier Analysis
- **Outlier formula card:** Displays Tukey's Lower Bound = Q1 - 1.5×IQR and Upper Bound = Q3 + 1.5×IQR
- **Total Bill outliers panel:**
  - Five-number summary (Min, Q1, Median, Q3, Max)
  - Lower and upper fence values
  - Detected high-value bill chips (individual outlier values)
- **Tip Amount outliers panel:** (same layout as above)
- **Complete Outlier Roster table:** All outlier events with Party ID, Bill, Tip, Tip%, Size, Day, Time, Smoker, Trigger (High Bill / High Tip / Both)

### Tab 4 · Visualizations Gallery (7 Distinct Plots)

All charts are rendered via Chart.js on `<canvas>` elements. Charts re-render on theme
toggle and when Tab 4 is first activated.

| # | Canvas ID        | Chart.js Type   | X Axis                | Y Axis              | Extra                       |
|---|------------------|-----------------|-----------------------|---------------------|-----------------------------|
| 1 | `chartHistogram` | `bar`           | Bill range bins (₹)   | Frequency (count)   | INR bins: ₹0–₹4400 in 12 bands |
| 2 | `chartScatter`   | `scatter`       | Total Bill (₹)        | Tip (₹)             | OLS trendline (type: 'line') overlay |
| 3 | `chartBoxplot`   | `bar` (stacked) | Day (Thur/Fri/Sat/Sun)| Bill (₹)            | IQR range bars + Median line overlay |
| 4 | `chartLine`      | `line`          | Party size (1–6)      | Average Bill (₹)    | Filled area, tension=0.2    |
| 5 | `chartBar`       | `bar`           | Day (Thu/Fri/Sat/Sun) | Visits (count)      | 4-color bars, no legend     |
| 6 | `chartPie`       | `doughnut`      | —                     | Day proportions (%) | Legend at bottom            |
| 7 | (HTML heatmap)   | CSS Grid (HTML) | 3 vars (row headers)  | 3 vars (col headers)| `.heat-100/.heat-68/.heat-60/.heat-49` CSS cells |

Gallery filter buttons let user isolate individual chart types (hist / scatter / box / line / bar / pie / heat).

### Tab 5 · Business Report & AI Findings
- **Revenue KPI cards:** Total Revenue, Average Customer Spend, Highest Single Bill
- **AI-Generated Business Report:** HTML injected from Gemini/OpenRouter/Groq into `#gemini-report-content`
  - Report structure: Customer Behavior & Key Findings | Actionable Recommendations
  - Formatted with `<h4>`, `<p>`, `<ul>/<li>`, `<strong>`
  - Loading spinner while waiting for API response

